3.3. Mesh method
The model mesh is generated in ANSYS Fluent using the Faulttolerant meshing workflow, which effectively handles unstructured grids for complex geometries. The volumetric mesh utilizes a PolyHexcore division, optimizing computational efficiency while ensuring high mesh quality in intricate regions. A three-layer boundary layer is applied at the fluid-solid interface, as shown in Fig. 6(a). Sensitivity testing involved seven different mesh sizes, as shown in Fig. 6(b), which revealed variations in the Nusselt number (Nu), friction factor (f), and performance evaluation coefficient (PEC) relative to mesh density. As the number of mesh elements increases, parameter deviations decrease, particularly when the mesh count exceeds four million. To balance accuracy and computational cost, a final mesh of approximately eight million elements was selected for the simulations.
