4. Results and discussion
The performance of regenerative cooling channels plays a critical role in determining the thermal management efficiency of propulsion systems. This section provides a comprehensive assessment of the cooling performance of all TPMS conformal channels by analyzing their flow and heat transfer characteristics, circumferential temperature uniformity, and overall performance, thereby elucidating the impact of conformal strategies on channel behavior.
4.1. Fluid flow and heat transfer characteristics
